;; Branch-aware Ring middleware.
;;
;; `:branch-routing-wrap` takes a `:fn`-typed `:base-handler` and
;; returns a Ring callable that dispatches per branch — header
;; `X-Graphden-Branch: <name>` or query `?branch=<name>` picks the
;; per-branch ExecutionContext, builds a fresh compiled registry on
;; first hit (cached), and runs the SAME compiled handler (here,
;; `:_app-ring-response`) against that branch's storage view.
;;
;; The wrap delegates to `graphden.system.branch-router/dispatch`.
;; When no active router is installed (startup before
;; `:exec/branch-router` init-key, test paths that strip the system
;; layer), the wrap calls the base-handler directly — graceful
;; fallback that matches single-branch behaviour.


{:namespace "web.branch-router"
 :description "Branch-aware Ring middleware — wraps a top-level Ring handler with per-branch dispatch."
 :fns
 [{:name :branch-routing-wrap
   :description "Per-request branch dispatcher. Receives the Ring request directly (free arg `:request`) plus a `:fn`-typed `:base-handler` (the main-branch handler used as fallback). Asks `graphden.system.branch-router/current-router` which branch to serve, then either runs `:base-handler` (no active router, or default branch) or delegates to the per-branch handler the router has cached."
   ;; `:base-handler` deliberately uses the loose `:fn` slot type
   ;; rather than a structural `[:fn {:request …} :ring-response-shape]`.
   ;; The type-checker's fn-def-as-callable model derives its
   ;; structural shape from the registry's `:args` map, which mixes
   ;; bound + free args (same shape `:router-ring-response` /
   ;; `:merge-in` produce). A tightened slot type would WARN on EVERY
   ;; fn-graph bound here even though runtime is well-formed (the impl
   ;; just does `(base-handler request)`, hof-wrap pads it). Matches
   ;; `:http-server.handler` which also stays loose for the same
   ;; reason. See `docs/VERSIONING.md` § Known gaps for the deeper
   ;; type-checker limitation.
   :args {:base-handler :fn
          :request {:type :ring-request-shape}}
   :return-type :ring-response-shape
   :effects #{:network}}]}
